{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MSmnsB4DTTL715och2rGCQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor Brownfield Discovery â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1, approved)\n2\t\n3\t## North Star (locked)\n4\tWhen an R&D project is registered or opened on an existing folder, Anchor instantly\n5\t(local, no tokens) discovers genuine pre-existing trio artifacts and adopts them so the\n6\tdashboard populates (home R&D panel + tile rollup + project Kanban) â€” honestly:\n7\tdiscovered items are excluded from the real effort count (shown as \"M imported\"), get\n8\tno `vN` label, are clickable to their real on-disk file, and carry a subtle `imported`\n9\tmarker. Anchor also writes `Anchor.md` (human, structure-only, no-churn) + a machine\n10\tsidecar describing the folder's R&D structure.\n11\t\n12\t## Approved decisions\n13\t- Marker = `Anchor.md` (human, regenerated) + a machine JSON sidecar.\n14\t- Discovered artifacts ADOPTED as efforts (so the existing tile/Kanban readers fill in)\n15\t  â€” but visibly, subtly labeled \"imported\" (user Stage-1 ruling: as understated as\n16\t  possible while honest), separately counted, never given fake provenance/`vN`.\n17\t- Scan on register + `/project/<id>` open + a manual Rescan button.\n18\t- Python stdlib only; integrate with `rnd_registry`/`lanes`/`effort_history`/`anchor_gui`\n19\t  + the Kanban window; keep the 236-test suite green; commit-safe.\n20\t\n21\t## Phasing â†’ see `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (7 waves)\n22\tScan â†’ honest data model + reconciliation â†’ render honesty â†’ file route + status line +\n23\thome panel â†’ marker writer â†’ wiring â†’ end-to-end gate.\n24\t\n25\t## Resolved risks (from two Shark-Tank rounds, code-verified)\n26\tProvenance honesty (source flag, no fake cost, excluded from count); `vN` would have\n27\tbroken the kanban test (compute over real efforts only); the `/artifact` route is a\n28\ttraversal risk (use the `katex_asset` containment pattern + negative tests); `Anchor.md`\n29\twrite-on-GET race (WRITE_LOCK + concurrency test); over-broad globs (provenance-signal\n30\tclassification); self-scan of `.anchor` (excluded); deletion/staleness (reconcile/prune\n31\tdiscovered records on rescan); home R&D panel must also fill in (in trigger+render set).\n32\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abf94295-ed6b-4c2f-b28a-703e6a4c4ac4","uuid":"60e4f9d8-d913-40f0-881c-6114172a417d","timestamp":"2026-06-13T18:03:33.739Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\brownfield-discovery\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor Brownfield Discovery â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1, approved)\n\n## North Star (locked)\nWhen an R&D project is registered or opened on an existing folder, Anchor instantly\n(local, no tokens) discovers genuine pre-existing trio artifacts and adopts them so the\ndashboard populates (home R&D panel + tile rollup + project Kanban) â€” honestly:\ndiscovered items are excluded from the real effort count (shown as \"M imported\"), get\nno `vN` label, are clickable to their real on-disk file, and carry a subtle `imported`\nmarker. Anchor also writes `Anchor.md` (human, structure-only, no-churn) + a machine\nsidecar describing the folder's R&D structure.\n\n## Approved decisions\n- Marker = `Anchor.md` (human, regenerated) + a machine JSON sidecar.\n- Discovered artifacts ADOPTED as efforts (so the existing tile/Kanban readers fill in)\n  â€” but visibly, subtly labeled \"imported\" (user Stage-1 ruling: as understated as\n  possible while honest), separately counted, never given fake provenance/`vN`.\n- Scan on register + `/project/<id>` open + a manual Rescan button.\n- Python stdlib only; integrate with `rnd_registry`/`lanes`/`effort_history`/`anchor_gui`\n  + the Kanban window; keep the 236-test suite green; commit-safe.\n\n## Phasing â†’ see `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (7 waves)\nScan â†’ honest data model + reconciliation â†’ render honesty â†’ file route + status line +\nhome panel â†’ marker writer â†’ wiring â†’ end-to-end gate.\n\n## Resolved risks (from two Shark-Tank rounds, code-verified)\nProvenance honesty (source flag, no fake cost, excluded from count); `vN` would have\nbroken the kanban test (compute over real efforts only); the `/artifact` route is a\ntraversal risk (use the `katex_asset` containment pattern + negative tests); `Anchor.md`\nwrite-on-GET race (WRITE_LOCK + concurrency test); over-broad globs (provenance-signal\nclassification); self-scan of `.anchor` (excluded); deletion/staleness (reconcile/prune\ndiscovered records on rescan); home R&D panel must also fill in (in trigger+render set).\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
