{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0154ZZqofBG8qkLE75nPmr3t","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor Brownfield Discovery + `Anchor.md` Marker â€” Implementation Plan\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 2 (converged after a Stage-1 and a Stage-2 Shark-Tank round, all\n4\t> findings code-verified). Foreman-ready: 7 waves, each with an orchestrator-gateable\n5\t> `done-when` + Given/When/Then. Product code is Python-stdlib-only. The full 236-test\n6\t> suite must stay green.\n7\t\n8\ttest-command: python -m pytest -q\n9\t\n10\t## North Star (locked)\n11\tWhen an R&D project is registered or opened on an existing folder, Anchor INSTANTLY\n12\t(local, no tokens, no agent) discovers genuine pre-existing trio artifacts and ADOPTS\n13\tthem so the dashboard POPULATES (home R&D panel + tile rollup + project Kanban fill in)\n14\tâ€” but HONESTLY: discovered items are excluded from the real `effort_count` (shown\n15\tseparately as \"M imported\"), get NO `vN` label, are clickable to their REAL on-disk\n16\tfile, and carry a SUBTLE `imported` marker (a small dot). Anchor also writes/maintains\n17\t`Anchor.md` (human, structure-only, no-churn) + a machine sidecar.\n18\t\n19\t## Honesty contract (the spine â€” every wave serves it)\n20\t- Discovered records carry `source=\"discovered\"`; real available metadata only\n21\t  (path, `mtime`â†’`created_at`, title, kind); **never** fabricated cost/tokens/session_id.\n22\t- `list_efforts` still RETURNS discovered records (render needs them); only the\n23\t  ROLLUP counters exclude them. Tile reads `N efforts Â· M imported Â· $X`.\n24\t- Discovered cards: subtle dot, no `vN`, clickable to the real file. Not masqueraded\n25\t  as Anchor-run sessions.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## Wave 1 â€” `brownfield_scan.py` (pure scanner/classifier, stdlib)\n30\tBounded walk (skip `.git`, `node_modules`, `_archive`, the project's own `.anchor`;\n31\tdepth cap ~6, file cap ~5000; ignore large binaries). Classify by **trio provenance\n32\tsignals**, not broad globs: `build`=`foreman-checkpoint.json`/`foreman.config.json`;\n33\t`planning`=`planning/**` trio docs (`*MASTER-PLAN*`,`*IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN*`,\n34\t`*EXECUTION-LOG*`,`*DECISION-LOG*`); `research`=`report.md`/`report.pdf` under a\n35\tresearch store / researchPrime markers; `deliverables`=declared outputs. Generic\n36\t`*.pdf`/`*PLAN*.md` â†’ low-confidence `docs` (listed, NOT adopted). Robust to a\n37\tmissing/huge/UNC/mistyped path (returns an empty `ScanResult`, never hangs/raises).\n38\tReturns `ScanResult{by_lane, docs, counts, generated_at}`.\n39\t- **done-when:** `tests/test_brownfield_scan.py` (planted-fixture + `@pytest.mark.parametrize`,\n40\t  house style of `test_distro_scan.py`) is green and asserts the FULL `ScanResult` with\n41\t  numeric `counts` for ALL these cases.\n42\t- **GWT:** GIVEN a fixtures folder containing `foreman-checkpoint.json`,\n43\t  `planning/MASTER-PLAN.md`, a root `FUNDING-PLAN.md`, a vendored `paper.pdf` under a\n44\t  dir named `research/`, and `.git/`+`.anchor/`+`node_modules/` subtrees, WHEN `scan()`\n45\t  runs, THEN checkpointâ†’`by_lane.build`, `MASTER-PLAN.md`â†’`by_lane.planning`,\n46\t  `FUNDING-PLAN.md`â†’`docs` (NOT adopted), `paper.pdf`â†’`docs` (NOT an effort), and the\n47\t  `.git`/`.anchor`/`node_modules` trees are skipped; `counts` match exactly.\n48\t\n49\t## Wave 2 â€” `effort_history` honest-discovery model + reconciliation\n50\tAdd `source=\"discovered\"` to pointer-records. `adopt_discovered(folder, pid, scan)`\n51\tcreates/updates records with a STABLE path-hash `job_id` (idempotent rescans),\n52\t`mtime`â†’`created_at`, title, real artifact rel-path; NO cost/tokens/session_id.\n53\t`list_efforts` STILL returns discovered records. `lane_rollup`/`project_rollup`\n54\tEXCLUDE `source=\"discovered\"` from `effort_count` and cost, and ADD a parallel\n55\t`discovered_count` (+`discovered_cost`=0). **Reconcile on rescan:** discovered records\n56\twhose artifact no longer exists on disk are PRUNED (they are derived, so safe to\n57\tremove â€” unlike real efforts, which are never touched).\n58\t- **done-when:** new tests green AND the existing `test_cost_rollup.py` 3/2/1\n59\t  `effort_count` assertions pass unchanged (they seed no discovered efforts).\n60\t- **GWT:** GIVEN 2 real + 3 discovered efforts, WHEN `project_rollup` runs, THEN\n61\t  `effort_count==2`, `discovered_count==3`, cost unchanged; AND adopting twice yields\n62\t  no duplicates; AND after a discovered artifact is deleted + rescan, its record is gone.\n63\t\n64\t## Wave 3 â€” render honesty (no security surface yet)\n65\tThread `is_discovered` + `artifact_path` through `_gather_project_efforts` into the\n66\teffort view. Compute `vN` over NON-discovered efforts only; discovered cards get an\n67\t`imported` marker (`data-discovered=\"1\"` + a small dot class), never a `vN`. Tile +\n68\tcost rollup render `N efforts Â· M imported Â· $X`.\n69\t- **done-when:** render tests green, machine-asserted (no human \"subtle\" judgement).\n70\t- **GWT:** GIVEN a project with 2 real research efforts AND 1 discovered planning doc,\n71\t  WHEN the window/tile render, THEN the real research cards still read `>v2<`/`>v1<`\n72\t  (existing test stays green), the discovered card contains `data-discovered=\"1\"` and\n73\t  NO `>v<` token, and the tile text contains `1 imported`.\n74\t\n75\t## Wave 4 â€” `/artifact` file route (security) + `status_line()` + home panel\n76\tNew `GET /artifact/<pid>?path=<rel>` serving a discovered artifact from the project\n77\tfolder, using the proven `report_viewer.katex_asset` containment pattern:\n78\t`target=(folder/rel).resolve()` then `target.relative_to(folder.resolve())` or 404;\n79\treject absolute `rel`, reject resolved paths under `.git`/`.anchor`, reject\n80\tsymlink-escape. Wire `rnd_registry.status_line()` to reflect adopted+real efforts per\n81\tlane. Ensure the HOME-dashboard R&D panel + tiles (not only the project window) reflect\n82\tadopted efforts.\n83\t- **done-when:** a REQUIRED negative test (mirroring `test_report_route_safety.py`)\n84\t  green AND a status-line test green AND the home view renders imported counts.\n85\t- **GWT:** GIVEN a discovered artifact at `planning/MASTER-PLAN.md`, WHEN\n86\t  `GET /artifact/<pid>?path=planning/MASTER-PLAN.md`, THEN 200 + the file bytes; WHEN\n87\t  `?path=../../secret`, `/etc/passwd`, `.git/config`, or a symlink-escape, THEN 400/404\n88\t  and zero bytes read; AND `status_line()['planning'] != 'none-yet'`; AND the home R&D\n89\t  panel tile shows `1 imported`.\n90\t\n91\t## Wave 5 â€” marker writer (`Anchor.md` + sidecar), lock-safe + no-churn\n92\t`write_anchor_md(folder)` renders `Anchor.md` at the folder root under\n93\t`paths.WRITE_LOCK`: project name(s) (one section per project sharing the folder),\n94\tper-lane counts (real + imported), deliverables, key RELATIVE paths, last-scanned â€”\n95\t**STRUCTURE ONLY, never file contents**. Hash-compare: rewrite only if changed.\n96\tMachine sidecar `.anchor/projects/<id>/discovery.json` = full `ScanResult`.\n97\t- **done-when:** commit-safety test (asserts no file-content/secret leakage in\n98\t  `Anchor.md`) green; no-churn test green; concurrency test (house style of\n99\t  `test_threading_locks.py`) green.\n100\t- **GWT:** GIVEN an unchanged folder, WHEN `/project/<id>` opened twice, THEN\n101\t  `Anchor.md` is not rewritten on the 2nd open (mtime stable); WHEN N threads open the\n102\t  same project concurrently, THEN exactly one consistent `Anchor.md` (no corruption).\n103\t\n104\t## Wave 6 â€” wiring (register + open + Rescan)\n105\tOne pipeline `discover_and_adopt(pid)`: scan â†’ adopt â†’ reconcile â†’ write marker;\n106\tidempotent, bounded, folder-path-robust. Call from `rnd_registry.add_project`\n107\t(register), the `/project/<id>` GET handler (open), and `POST /api/rnd/rescan {id}`\n108\t(+ a **Rescan** button on the project window, the project tile, and the home R&D panel).\n109\t- **done-wh