{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GJzBWZt7ArsTkrMBRmyB9G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary grounded in the three member documents (Master Plan, Implementation Plan, Execution Log):\n\n## Anchor Brownfield Discovery â€” Grounded Session Summary\n\n**Goal / North Star (locked)**\n- When an R&D project is registered or opened on an existing folder, Anchor instantly discovers genuine pre-existing trio artifacts â€” **locally, with no tokens and no agent** â€” and adopts them so the dashboard populates (home R&D panel + tile rollup + project Kanban).\n- Adoption is **honest**: discovered items are excluded from the real `effort_count` (shown separately as \"M imported\"), get **no `vN` label**, are clickable to their real on-disk file, and carry a **subtle `imported` marker** (a small dot).\n- Anchor also writes/maintains `Anchor.md` (human-readable, **structure-only, no-churn**) plus a machine JSON sidecar.\n\n**Approved Stage-1 decisions**\n- Marker = `Anchor.md` (regenerated) + a machine JSON sidecar.\n- Discovered artifacts are adopted as efforts (so existing tile/Kanban readers fill in) but subtly labeled \"imported,\" separately counted, **never given fake provenance or `vN`** (user ruling: as understated as possible while honest).\n- Scan triggers on **register + `/project/<id>` open + a manual Rescan button**.\n- Python stdlib only; integrate with `rnd_registry`/`lanes`/`effort_history`/`anchor_gui` + the Kanban window; keep the **236-test suite green**; commit-safe.\n\n**The honesty contract (the spine)**\n- Discovered records carry `source=\"discovered\"` with real metadata only (path, `mtime`â†’`created_at`, title, kind) â€” **never** fabricated cost/tokens/session_id.\n- `list_efforts` still returns discovered records (render needs them); only the **rollup counters** exclude them. Tile reads `N efforts Â· M imported Â· $X`.\n\n**Implementation plan â€” 7 Foreman-ready waves** (each with an orchestrator-gateable `done-when` + Given/When/Then)\n1. `brownfield_scan.py` â€” pure stdlib scanner/classifier; bounded walk (depth â‰¤6, files â‰¤5000), skips `.git`/`node_modules`/`_archive`/`.anchor`; classifies by **trio provenance signals, not broad globs**; robust to missing/huge/UNC/mistyped paths (returns empty `ScanResult`, never hangs/raises).\n2. `effort_history` honest-discovery model + reconciliation â€” `adopt_discovered` (stable path-hash job_id, idempotent), rollups exclude discovered, **prune discovered records when their artifact is deleted** (real efforts never touched).\n3. Render honesty â€” thread `is_discovered` + `artifact_path`; `vN` computed over non-discovered only; discovered cards get `data-discovered=\"1\"` + dot.\n4. `/artifact/<pid>?path=<rel>` route (security) + `status_line()` + home panel â€” uses the proven `report_viewer.katex_asset` containment pattern; rejects traversal/absolute/`.git`/`.anchor`/symlink-escape.\n5. `Anchor.md` marker writer + sidecar â€” under `WRITE_LOCK`, hash-compare no-churn, structure-only.\n6. Wiring â€” one `discover_and_adopt(pid)` pipeline (scanâ†’adoptâ†’reconcileâ†’write marker) called from register, open, and Rescan.\n7. End-to-end live verify + full-suite gate.\n\n**Resolved risks (two Shark-Tank rounds, code-verified)**\n- Provenance honesty (source flag, no fake cost, excluded from count); `vN` would have broken the Kanban test (compute over real efforts only); `/artifact` traversal risk; `Anchor.md` write-on-GET race (WRITE_LOCK + concurrency test); over-broad globs; self-scan of `.anchor`; deletion/staleness (reconcile/prune); home panel must also fill in.\n\n**Build outcome (Execution Log â€” all 7 waves PASS)**\n- Every wave landed as designed: scanner (18 tests), discovery model (6 tests), render honesty (3 tests), `/artifact` safety (14 pass, 1 skip â€” symlink needs admin), marker writer (7 tests, 24-thread concurrency clean), wiring (3 live-server tests), and the final gate.\n- **Final full-suite gate: `python -m pytest -q` â†’ 284 passed, 1 skipped** (baseline 236 unchanged + 48 new; **no existing test weakened or deleted**).\n- Live HTTP smoke (throwaway server, port 0 â€” never 8777, no live `claude`) passed: home panel shows imported counts, project window shows discovered cards (no `vN`, `/artifact` links, imported marker), an incidental vendored `paper.pdf` is **not** adopted (listed in sidecar docs only), `/artifact` opens the real file while traversal attempts all return 404 with zero leak, rescan prunes a deleted artifact, and `Anchor.md` is structure-only (no secrets, no prose body).\n- distro build clean: ships `brownfield_scan.py` + `anchor_marker.py`; staged scan has no personal-data hits.\n\n**Note on a discrepancy worth flagging:** the implementation plan's `done-when` gates targeted \"â‰¥236 tests green,\" and the build reports 284 passed. The titles you supplied match the on-disk docs exactly, so this summary is grounded in the actual files rather than the anchor text alone â€” the one substantive thing the anchors omitted is that the build is **complete and GREEN**, not merely approved at Stage 1."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_read_input_tokens":57215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abf94295-ed6b-4c2f-b28a-703e6a4c4ac4","uuid":"0f47e7a1-9370-4436-9799-7c2f12b993e6","request_id":"req_011Cc1hYGF1w4RAHvFJYLj64"}
